d 2026-09-04 on merges into fleet/builder-permissions and bead/spot-2ig) and nothing revisits already-closed beads; added --audit over closed beads, and escalated the fleet-side closer fw-y1y which this repo cannot reach.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 2"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ke5FHoEP2kQniCoP4iBdLX","tool_input":{"command":"FLYWHEEL_AGENT=spotify-recsys-ecosystem/builder tools/flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=security file=scripts/reconcile_board.py line=42 severity=medium claim=\"RELEASED_REF was the bare refname 'origin/main', which gitrevisions resolves as a tag or local branch ahead of the remote-tracking ref, so a pushed tag could choose what counts as shipped; now refs/remotes/origin/main.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 3"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GsPYd5YD9sTj7B4tMKQ8Un","tool_input":{"command":"FLYWHEEL_AGENT=spotify-recsys-ecosystem/builder tools/flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=correctness file=scripts/reconcile_board.py line=155 severity=medium claim=\"verdict_for returned on the first non-merged PR, so a bead naming a superseded PR plus a genuinely stranded one held silently with no note forever; every PR is now judged before a verdict is returned and a strand outranks a hold.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 4"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01V4ZrfjJxnPg5hW7cqfgXkP","tool_input":{"command":"FLYWHEEL_AGENT=spotify-recsys-ecosystem/builder tools/flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=correctness+simplicity file=scripts/reconcile_board.py line=350 severity=medium claim=\"Two lenses flagged that skip and hold verdicts produced no row and no counter, so the summary read '13 beads, 0 closed, 0 stranded, 1 in flight' with twelve unaccounted; the Report now files every bead under exactly one heading and the counts add up.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 5"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvXCX4f6vjQGmjYNUWg9PF","tool_input":{"command":"FLYWHEEL_AGENT=spotify-recsys-ecosystem/builder tools/flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=security file=scripts/reconcile_board.py line=86 severity=medium claim=\"PR titles and branch names, which are author-controlled and editable after merge, were written verbatim into bead close reasons and the run log where other agents read them; _flatten now strips non-printables, collapses to one line and caps length.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 6"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BtmJMttQ2aVnak5F6T2Hxb","tool_input":{"command":"FLYWHEEL_AGENT=spotify-recsys-ecosystem/builder tools/flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=security file=scripts/reconcile_board.py line=170 severity=medium claim=\"The stranded note's only stated remedy was 'until that branch merges forward', an action ADR 0003 reserves to the human, addressed to whichever unattended agent read it; reworded to name the human as the merge authority.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 7"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqV3crQ8MLkLTfrjRSjnW6","tool_input":{"command":"FLYWHEEL_AGENT=spotify-recsys-ecosystem/builder tools/flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=security file=scripts/reconcile_board.py line=272 severity=medium claim=\"bead_id reached bd's argv in flag position with no separator, and bd close with no positional id closes the last touched issue, so a dash-leading id could force-close an unrelated bead; calls are now 'bd close --reason X -- <id>' and 'bd note -- <id> <text>'.\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 8"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EKhoKqf7Ta3RXm2KYTddh4","tool_input":{"command":"git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nspot-e11: close a bead only when its merge reached main\n\nreconcile-board treated \"gh says MERGED\" as \"the work shipped\". Those are\nthe same thing only when the PR's base is the released branch, and on\n2026-08-30 they were not: spot-2ig closed on PR #4, whose base was\nfleet/builder-permissions, and its work sat off main for a day.\n\nscripts/reconcile_board.py resolves each PR's baseRefName and merge commit\nand closes only when that commit is an ancestor of refs/remotes/origin/main.\nA merge that landed anywhere else leaves the bead open with a note naming\nthe branch. Every unknown -- an unresolvable PR, a merge with no merge\ncommit, a commit this clone has never fetched -- holds rather than closes.\n\nTwo things the live board taught the design. `bd list --status=open` skips\nin_progress, which is the status of every bead with a PR in review, so it\nfiltered out exactly the beads to reconcile; and a bead's notes may cite\nsomebody else's PR as a precondition (spot-24j does), so the reference must\nbe the anchored line step 7 writes and the PR must be the bead's own work,\nby branch or by title.\n\n--audit asks the same question of already-closed beads and only reports:\nwhether the work is on main is a fact, but reopening is a judgement and\nmerging is the human's call (ADR 0003).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" -- scripts","description":"Commit the reconcile-board module and tests"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CjV1kJ4ZmDQRBFmcKufnYT","tool_input":{"command":"git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F /tmp/spot-e11-msg1.txt -- scripts","description":"Commit reconcile-board module and tests"}},{"tool_name":"mcp__blackbird__blackbird_conversation_open","tool_use_id":"toolu_015S1mRhskVa3EdY6BWwCy63","tool_input":{"agent_token":"bbm_f4efdfe5d85c4db16b707e0eb75432de56829f02087e40da16299b8aed24539c","topic":"escalate: spot-e11 defect recurred — two closed beads are off main"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_012x2hfETkYwBuysefLzEQuF","tool_input":{"command":"until [ \"$(gh pr checks 12 --json name,state --jq '.[] | select(.name==\"lint\") | .state')\" != \"PENDING\" ]; do sleep 15; done; gh pr checks 12 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Wait for lint check to finish","run_in_background":true}},{"tool_name":"Monitor","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TEiscJJckGYrw37LGPHP1Y","tool_input":{"description":"PR 12 lint check outcome","timeout_ms":900000,"persistent":false,"command":"while true; do s=$(gh pr checks 12 --json name,state --jq 'map(select(.name==\"lint\"))[0].state'); if [ \"$s\" != \"PENDING\" ]; then echo \"lint: $s\"; break; fi; sleep 20; done"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_0165vAWoNprMcDbVJuxRXcjq","tool_input":{"command":"gh run watch 33924053244 --exit-status --compact 2>&1 | tail -15","description":"Watch the CI run to completion","run_in_background":true}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014XAi1nmRwVwB6J692wcJJz","tool_input":{"command":"gh run watch 33924053244 --exit-status --compact","description":"Watch the CI run to completion","run_in_background":true}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":3},"started_in_background":3,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":93,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. **PR #12** is open and green: https://github.com/jamesponwith/spotify-recsys-ecosystem/pull/12\n\n**Bead:** spot-e11 (P0 bug) — close-on-merge must check the merge target. Left open, labelled `w:3`, until you merge.\n\n**What I built.** `scripts/reconcile_board.py` resolves each PR's `baseRefName` and merge commit through `gh` and closes a bead only when that commit is an ancestor of `refs/remotes/origin/main`. A merge that landed elsewhere leaves the bead open with a note naming the branch. Every unknown holds. `--audit` asks the same question of already-closed beads and only reports. Wired into `make` and a new CI job, since `scripts/` had no test gate at all.\n\n**The bead's defect recurred while I was working on it.** The fleet's closer (`fw-y1y`) closed two more beads today on merges that never reached main — spot-7lj (PR #9 → `fleet/builder-permissions`) and spot-4gd (PR #10 → `bead/spot-2ig`). Both verified with `merge-base --is-ancestor`. spot-4gd matters beyond itself: spot-yld depends on it, so the board currently shows spot-yld ready when its foundation isn't on main.\n\n**I could not fix the tool that did this** — `fw-y1y` lives in the flywheel repo, outside this worktree. Filed as **spot-3wy** (P0, labelled `human`). It needs your decision on how those two merges reach main; the fleet doesn't merge.\n\n**Gate.** `make lint-all` green, 25 scripts tests, all five app suites pass. CI: 7/7 checks pass.\n\n**Self-review (ADR 0013).** Three lenses, 24 findings recorded in `.flywheel/review.jsonl` — 17 accepted, 7 rejected with reasons. The one worth the whole exercise: the bead↔PR binding was unauthenticated free text, so one appended `PR #N opened` line on untouched work would have retired it the moment someone else's PR landed. Now the PR must be the bead's own, by branch or title.\n\n**Two things I left out deliberately:** reopening the stranded beads and merging those branches forward (yours under ADR 0003), and scheduling this tool — nothing runs it on a timer, and that's a separate idea from getting the decision right.\n\nTwo caveats worth your attention: blackbird's messaging tools needed an interactive permission grant I can't make here, so the escalation went through the beads `human` label rather than an ack-required message; and I left the worktree in place rather than removing it, since I'm running inside it.","ttft_ms":37043,"type":"result","duration_ms":572004,"uuid":"b45bc861-88af-435b-b47b-22c03e38ee08","ttft_stream_ms":938,"time_to_request_ms":28,"queued_turn_count":0}
